json/string
description: Double-quoted string
- >
  A string is a sequence of Unicode characters enclosed into double quotes. Special characters
  ride behind a backslash — `\"`, `\\`, `\/`, `\b`, `\f`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, and `\uXXXX` for an
  arbitrary code unit. Literal line breaks inside a string are not allowed — a JSON string always
  fits one line:
- !!<format: text/x-json> |
  "line one\nline \"two\"\tand a tab"
